      {
        "id": 145577,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-07-28T04:01:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Unrelenting Momentum will allow a free usage of LSB, but the timing of the free use renders it useless.</p><p>As Luther stated, and I can't find anything overruling it, when you use an ability the second time you immediately have the option to do it a third time for free. &nbsp;You can choose to do it again or not, but it must be right then. &nbsp;You cannot use any ability inbetween.</p><p>So your free LSB will doubly ensure that your next attack uses dice equal to your movement.</p><p>It will have no actual effect, the next attack will be affected by both LSB uses, which is no different than being affected by one.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:22.067Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
